Revision history for Google::gRPC

0.09    2026-11-23
    - Overhauled POD documentation (modeled on grpc.io language docs) across Google::gRPC and all submodules: Client, Channel, ChannelPool, Engine, Engine::NGHTTP2, Engine::PP, Stream, Deadline, Status, and Framing.
    - Added META_MERGE resources in Makefile.PL for CPAN and Debian upstream/metadata compliance.

0.08    2026-11-22
    - Fixed CPAN/PAUSE indexing metadata in Makefile.PL (LICENSE => 'apache_2_0', VERSION_FROM => 'lib/Google/gRPC.pm').
    - Cleaned compiled artifacts (gRPC.bs, NGHTTP2.c, NGHTTP2.o) and tmp/ scratch files from MANIFEST.

0.07    2026-11-21
    - Hardened NGHTTP2.xs session lifecycle, data source tracking, callback error capture (G_EVAL), and header/trailer classification.
    - Added GOOGLE_CLOUD_QUOTA_PROJECT header support.
    - Removed duplicate xs/NGHTTP2.xs and updated MANIFEST.

0.06    Tue Jul 28 2026
    - Added SECURITY.md

0.05    2026-07-27
        - Exclude BUILD from POD coverage tests.
        - Resolved author testing failures (Kwalitee, PerlTidy).
        - Updated RT bug tracker URLs, repository links, and author email in Makefile.PL.

0.04    Wed Jul 22 2026
        [POD Documentation & Quality Modernization]
        - Added comprehensive POD documentation (NAME, SYNOPSIS, DESCRIPTION, AUTHOR, LICENSE) across all Google::gRPC submodules.
        - Added main package module Google::gRPC.pm ($VERSION = 0.04) and t/99-pod-coverage.t test suite.

0.03    Fri Jul 17 2026
        [Engine Architecture & Cross-Platform Support]
        - Hardened C/XS NGHTTP2 transport engine configuration and added dynamic fallback to Pure-Perl Protocol::HTTP2 engine when libnghttp2 development headers are absent.
        - Updated Makefile.PL auto-detection for cross-platform Linux, macOS, and Windows runners.

        [Architecture & CPAN Cleanup]
        - Upgraded package version to 0.03 (lib/Google/gRPC/Client.pm and lib/Google/gRPC/Engine/NGHTTP2.pm).
        - Pruned redundant $VERSION declarations from sub-module files.

0.02    2026-06-24
        - Extracted from Google::Auth distribution into its own standalone package.
        - Enforced strict Single Responsibility Principle (SRP) separation.
